# MCSP Controlled Kernel Execution 0.57

Status: Constructive isolated-runtime experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parents:
- DRIVER-CONSTRUCTION-FIXTURE-0.56.mcsp
- KBUILD-MODULE-INTEGRATION-0.54.mcsp
- QEMU EDU DMA witness 0.35

## Objective

Execute the bounded 0.56 driver artifact only inside a disposable QEMU Linux guest
with the QEMU EDU PCI device attached.

The host kernel SHALL NOT load the MCSP module.

## Architecture

    MCSP KERNEL = DETERMINATE CONDITION
        -> report-derived driver construction
        -> Linux .ko realization
        -> disposable QEMU guest kernel
        -> module insertion inside guest
        -> PCI probe evidence
        -> guest termination

Linux remains an external realization kernel.

## 0.57 runtime boundary

Guest:
- QEMU x86-64;
- matching Debian kernel;
- QEMU EDU device 1234:11e8;
- disposable initramfs;
- no persistent guest disk required;
- serial evidence captured by host.

The 0.56 probe performs identity qualification only. It does not enable PCI,
map MMIO, execute DMA, register IRQs, or mutate device registers.

## Qualification events

The isolated runtime shall evidence:
1. guest kernel boot;
2. EDU PCI device enumeration;
3. module insertion attempt inside guest only;
4. module init/probe result;
5. MCSP bounded identity predicate participates in probe;
6. no host module insertion;
7. deterministic guest termination.

## Boundary

Actual MMIO, DMA, IRQ handling, device mutation, production deployment, and host
kernel insertion remain outside 0.57.
